@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;security] windows-editor-native-fixture-boundary
The harness MUST require an explicitly isolated Windows VM, the source-built
candidate and a real current Lyra-authorized canonical SAM account. Its fixed
account relay MUST bind only loopback and reject browser requests to other
origins. It MUST NOT create or weaken production admission, substitute an
authorizer, or count administrative SSH as ordinary CLI acceptance.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;recovery] windows-editor-native-recovery-evidence
Acceptance MUST observe native workbench/extension/terminal behavior and exact
SAM SID, executable, PID and creation-time custody. Broker loss MUST retain the
worker and saved file; worker loss MUST produce a distinct process with the
same account and saved file. Static checks or harness packaging MUST NOT count
as native execution, fleet authorization or capability promotion.
